    <header>
        <h1>Research Proposal</h1>
        <p>Project ID: #AID-2024-BETA</p>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2>Project Title</h2>
        <p><strong>"Project <span class="highlight">Atlantis</span>: An Integrated Neuro-Adaptive Interface for Enhancing Autonomy in Persons with Physical Disabilities."</strong></p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>1. Abstract</h2>
        <p>
            Current assistive technologies often lack the intuitive feedback required for seamless integration into daily life. This research project seeks to develop a novel, non-invasive neural-sensory feedback loop. By leveraging the conceptual framework of "deep-sea immersion" and environmental stability, much like the legendary lost city of <span class="highlight">atlantis</span>, this research aims to create an "underwater" layer of digital support—a stable, immersive environment where technology feels like a natural extension of the body rather than an external tool.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>2. Problem Statement</h2>
        <p>
            For individuals with severe motor impairments, "quality of life" is frequently hindered by the high cognitive load required to operate standard assistive devices. Furthermore, there is a significant gap in the enforcement of accessibility standards in municipal and private urban sectors, often leaving the implementation of accessibility laws un-checked and un-verified.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>3. Methodology & Objectives</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Objective A:</strong> Development of the "Fluid Interface," using bio-feedback to reduce the cognitive strain of device operation.</li>
            <li><strong>Objective B:</strong> Implementation of an AI-driven <span class="highlight">constable</span> for Accessibility Compliance. This software module will act as a digital monitor, proactively scanning local digital environments and physical hardware settings to ensure they meet real-time accessibility requirements.</li>
            <li><strong>Objective C:</strong> Longitudinal study to measure psychological well-being and sense of agency in a controlled cohort of 150 participants.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>4. Expected Impact</h2>
        <p>
            The successful completion of Project Atlantis will move the needle from "assistive technology" (which implies helping someone overcome a deficit) to "integrated technology" (which implies expanding human capability). When the digital <span class="highlight">constable</span> functions alongside the fluid interface, users will experience a significant increase in spontaneous social interaction and reduced home-bound isolation.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>5. Resources & Budget</h2>
        <p>Required: Neuro-imaging equipment, haptic feedback components, and a multi-disciplinary team consisting of neurologists, UX designers, and legal ethics specialists. Total projected budget: $1.2M.</p>
    </section>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2024 Institute for Human-Centric Technology</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>

